      }
    ],
    "conclusion": "1. Lung-RADS category 2: benign appearance or behavior. 4 mm solid right middle lobe nodule, stable since 10/02/2025. Continue annual screening with low-dose CT in 12 months.\n2. S: Moderate coronary artery calcification. Clinical correlation for cardiovascular risk management is recommended.\n3. Mild centrilobular emphysema.",
    "presentedForm": [
      {
        "contentType": "text/plain",
        "text": "EXAM:\nCT CHEST, LOW-DOSE LUNG CANCER SCREENING\n\nCLINICAL INDICATION:\nAnnual lung cancer screening. Asymptomatic. Former smoker, 30 pack-years, quit 2018.\n\nTECHNIQUE:\nLow-dose helical CT of the chest was performed without intravenous contrast. Axial images were reconstructed at 1 mm with coronal and sagittal reformats. CTDIvol: 1.4 mGy. DLP: 52 mGy-cm.\n\nCOMPARISON:\nLow-dose CT chest dated 10/02/2025.\n\nFINDINGS:\nLungs: 4 mm solid nodule in the right middle lobe (series 4, image 88), unchanged from 10/02/2025. No new or growing nodules. Mild centrilobular emphysema. No consolidation. The airways are patent.\nPleura: No pleural effusion or pneumothorax.\nHeart and mediastinum: Heart size is normal. Moderate coronary artery calcification involving the left anterior descending and right coronary arteries. No mediastinal lymphadenopathy.\nLower neck: 11 mm hypodense nodule in the right thyroid lobe.\nUpper abdomen: Unremarkable on this limited noncontrast exam.\nBones: Mild degenerative changes of the thoracic spine.\n\nIMPRESSION:\n1. Lung-RADS category 2: benign appearance or behavior. 4 mm solid right middle lobe nodule, stable since 10/02/2025. Continue annual screening with low-dose CT in 12 months.\n2. S: Moderate coronary artery calcification. Clinical correlation for cardiovascular risk management is recommended.\n3. Mild centrilobular emphysema."
      }
    ]
  },
